# Task 1 - Distributed web infrastructure

A user wants to open www.foobar.com in their browser:

1. The browser asks DNS for the IP address of www.foobar.com.
2. DNS answers with 8.8.8.8, the IP of the load balancer.
3. The browser sends an HTTP request to 8.8.8.8.
4. HAProxy chooses one of the two servers (round robin) and forwards the
   request to its Nginx web server.
5. Nginx serves static files itself and forwards dynamic requests to the
   application server. The application server runs the code base and talks to
   MySQL: writes go to the Primary, reads can go to the Replica.
6. The response goes back through the load balancer to the user.

## Infrastructure

- 3 servers in total: Server 1, Server 2 and Server 3 (the load balancer)
- Server 3: 1 load balancer (HAProxy), IP 8.8.8.8
- Server 1: 1 web server (Nginx), 1 application server, 1 set of application
  files (code base), 1 MySQL database (Primary)
- Server 2: 1 web server (Nginx), 1 application server, 1 set of application
  files (code base), 1 MySQL database (Replica)
- 1 domain name: foobar.com, with a www A record pointing to 8.8.8.8

